{{!
    @template local_unifiedgrader/help_section_quiz

    Help page partial: marking a quiz. The grader's help button links to
    #integration-quiz, so that id must stay.

    Context variables:
    * img - object - Screenshot URLs keyed by file name in pix/help.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "img": {
            "quiz": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/quiz",
            "quiz_due_date": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/quiz_due_date",
            "quiz_late_penalty": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/quiz_late_penalty"
        }
    }
}}
<section id="integration-quiz" class="local-unifiedgrader-help-activity">
<h4 class="local-unifiedgrader-help-activity-title"><i class="fa fa-check-square-o" aria-hidden="true"></i> Quizzes</h4>

<p>Use the grader to mark the questions Moodle cannot mark for you, such as essays, and to give
feedback on the attempt as a whole.</p>

<h5>What you see</h5>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Left:</strong> the student's attempt, question by question, in the order they saw
        it. Automatically marked questions show their result. Moodle's own
        <em>Make comment or override mark</em> link appears under each question.</li>
    <li><strong>Right:</strong> a <strong>Manually marked questions</strong> list with one row per
        question that needs you: a score box and a comment editor. The badge shows how many are done (<em>0 / 1</em>).</li>
    <li>Below that, <strong>Overall Feedback</strong> for the attempt and the usual notes.</li>
    <li>When a student has more than one finished attempt, an attempt selector appears. Feedback is kept per attempt.</li>
</ul>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.quiz}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.quiz}}" width="1600" height="909" loading="lazy"
             alt="A quiz attempt. On the left, an essay question with the student's answer and a true/false question marked correct. On the right, a Manually marked questions list with a score box and comment editor for question 1.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>A quiz with an essay question. The essay gets a score and a comment on the right.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h5>Mark a question</h5>
<ol>
    <li>Read the answer in the preview.</li>
    <li>Type the score in the question's score box. A score above the question's maximum, or below zero, is refused.</li>
    <li>Write a comment if you wish. It can hold formatting, images and recorded audio.</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Save feedback</strong>. Moodle recalculates the quiz grade.</li>
</ol>
<p>The score box of a question worth zero marks is disabled; the question can still take a comment. The overall grade box
is filled by Moodle from the question marks.</p>

<h5>Due date, late attempts and extensions</h5>
<p>In Moodle 5.3 a quiz has its own <strong>Due date</strong> in its <em>Timing</em> settings,
separate from the date it closes. A quiz without a due date is never late.</p>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.quiz_due_date}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.quiz_due_date}}" width="1300" height="323" loading="lazy"
             alt="The Timing section of the quiz settings: Open the quiz, Due date (enabled), Close the quiz, Time limit and When time expires.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>The quiz <strong>Due date</strong> is a standard Moodle 5.3 quiz setting.</figcaption>
</figure>

<p>With <em>Apply late penalties</em> ticked for the quiz, the student's <strong>first real
attempt</strong> decides whether the quiz is late. A real attempt is one where they answered at
least half of the questions (your administrator can change that share).</p>
<ul>
    <li>First real attempt on time: no penalty, even if later attempts come after the due date.</li>
    <li>First real attempt late: the penalty for that lateness comes off the quiz grade, whatever later attempts score.</li>
</ul>
<p>The grader shows the lateness and the penalty as it does for an assignment
(see <a href="#feature-penalties">Penalties</a>). To excuse a student, extend their due date in
<a href="#feature-overrides">Dates &amp; extensions</a>.</p>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot local-unifiedgrader-help-shot-narrow">
    <a href="{{img.quiz_late_penalty}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.quiz_late_penalty}}" width="1200" height="750" loading="lazy"
             alt="The marking panel on a late quiz attempt: a banner reading Late: 1 day 23 hours, and a red badge reading minus 10 percent, 2 days late, under the grade box.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>A late quiz attempt: the exact lateness in the banner, the penalty in the badge.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h5>Posting quiz grades</h5>
<p>A quiz normally shows marks according to its <em>Review options</em>. If your administrator has
switched on <em>Enable post grades for quizzes</em>, the
<a href="#feature-post-grades">post-grades control</a> also works on quizzes, with some
differences explained there.</p>

<p>On a proctored quiz, see <a href="#feature-proctoring">Proctoring results</a>.</p>
</section>
